# MCP — project tooling

Shared config: `.cursor/mcp.json`

| Name | Target |
|------|--------|
| `supabase-prod` | `mnytrlcmdpkfhrzrtesf` |
| `supabase-staging` | `ttjtyvxfiqhjdngkgdkf` |
| `github` | `https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/` |
| `posthog` | `https://mcp.posthog.com/mcp` |

- If those servers are missing in a Cloud Agent, tell the user to follow `docs/MCP_SETUP.md` (dashboard HTTP servers + OAuth/PAT). Do not pretend MCP is available when only `cursor-cloud` is listed.
- Prefer MCP for live DB work when present; keep matching files under `supabase/`. Say clearly whether a change targets **staging** or **prod**.
- Prefer PostHog MCP for analytics/flags/error investigation when present; keep app keys in gitignored `.env*.local`.
- Never commit PATs or put raw secrets in `.cursor/mcp.json`; use `${env:GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN}` (and `GITHUB_PAT`) or dashboard encrypted headers.
